---
import DocShell from '../../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../../lib/nav';

const toc = [
   { id: 'install', label: 'Install' },
   { id: 'test', label: 'Test API' },
   { id: 'driver', label: 'Driver sessions' },
   { id: 'axe', label: 'axe' },
   { id: 'wcag', label: 'WCAG lookup' },
   { id: 'inspect', label: 'Applicability' },
   { id: 'doctor', label: 'Diagnostics' },
   { id: 'exports', label: 'Export map' },
   { id: 'packages', label: 'Packages' },
];
---

<DocShell
   title="TypeScript API"
   summary="Import the screen reader test API from a11ied/test, the Vitest matchers and the queued sr fixture from a11ied/vitest, and driver sessions, axe runs, WCAG lookups, applicability, and host diagnostics from the a11ied package. These are the same functions the CLI commands and the MCP tools call."
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section class="split panel" id="install">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Install</p>
            <h2>Install into a project</h2>
         </div>
         <pre><code>npm install a11ied</code></pre>
         <p>
            The package ships ESM with type declarations and four entry points:
            <code>a11ied</code>, <code>a11ied/test</code>, <code>a11ied/vitest</code>, and
            <code>a11ied/browser</code>. Internal file paths are not part of the public API and
            change between releases.
         </p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">Errors</div>
         <p class="aside-note">
            Failures throw <code>CliUsageError</code> for bad input,
            <code>CliEnvironmentError</code> for a missing browser or target, and
            <code>DriverCommandError</code> for an unresolvable command name. All three are
            exported, so <code>instanceof</code> works.
         </p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="test">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Tests</p>
         <h2>Drive a screen reader from a test</h2>
      </div>
      <pre><code>import {'{'} queuedScreenReader {'}'} from 'a11ied/test';

await using sr = await queuedScreenReader({'{'} url: 'http://localhost:3000/checkout' {'}'});

sr.goTo({'{'} role: 'button', name: 'Pay' {'}'});
sr.activate();
sr.expectSpoken(/order placed/iu);</code></pre>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><code>screenReader(options?)</code><span>Takes <code>sr</code>, <code>url</code> or <code>html</code>, <code>mode</code> (<code>in-process</code> by default, or <code>broker</code>), <code>engine</code>, <code>recordingPath</code>, <code>idleTimeoutMinutes</code>, and <code>timeoutMs</code>. Returns a <code>ScreenReader</code> with the page open. Every method returns a promise.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><div class="route-terms"><code>queuedScreenReader(options?, queue?)</code>, <code>queueScreenReader(reader, queue?)</code></div><span>The same options, and a <code>QueuedScreenReader</code> instead. <code>queueScreenReader</code> wraps a <code>ScreenReader</code> that is already started.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>QueuedScreenReader</code><span>Every <code>ScreenReader</code> method except <code>stop</code>, with the same parameters, returning a <code>Queued&lt;T&gt;</code> thenable instead of a <code>Promise&lt;T&gt;</code>. A call queues a command and returns at once, and the queued commands run one at a time in the order they were queued. Awaiting a call runs the commands queued before it, then that one, and gives its value. <code>session</code> is a plain property, <code>reader</code> is the underlying <code>ScreenReader</code>, <code>drain()</code> waits for every queued command, and <code>stop()</code> drains, stops the reader even when the drain failed, then rethrows that error. <code>await using</code> calls <code>stop()</code>.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>CommandQueueOptions</code><span>The second argument to both. <code>track(settled)</code> receives one promise per command, which rejects only when the command failed and nothing awaited it. <code>signal</code>, an <code>AbortSignal</code>, skips every command not yet started once it aborts. The <code>a11ied/vitest</code> fixture passes both, and a test needs neither.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>ScreenReader</code><span><code>next</code>, <code>previous</code>, <code>press</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>read</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>find</code>, <code>goTo</code>, <code>elements</code>, <code>readAll</code>, <code>walk</code>, <code>wait</code>, <code>checkpoint</code>, <code>transcript</code>, <code>open</code>, <code>interact</code>, <code>stopInteracting</code>, <code>activate</code>, <code>top</code>, <code>bottom</code>, <code>escape</code>, <code>table</code>, <code>perform</code>, <code>screenshot</code>, <code>focus</code>, <code>expectSpoken</code>, <code>expectCursorOn</code>, <code>expectSpokenInOrder</code>, <code>stop</code>, and <code>Symbol.asyncDispose</code>. Navigation methods return the phrase, and <code>read</code> returns a <code>DriverCurrentItem</code>.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>ScreenReaderAssertionError</code><span>Thrown by <code>expectSpoken</code>, <code>expectCursorOn</code>, <code>expectSpokenInOrder</code>, <code>wait</code>, <code>find</code>, and <code>goTo</code>. Has <code>expected</code>, <code>phrases</code>, and <code>exitCode: 4</code>.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>a11ied/vitest</code><span>Re-exports the above, installs <code>toHaveSpoken</code>, <code>toHaveSpokenInOrder</code>, and <code>toHaveCursorOn</code> on <code>expect</code>, and exports a <code>test</code> whose <code>sr</code> fixture is a <code>QueuedScreenReader</code>, started from <code>srOptions</code> and stopped after each test. It needs Vitest 4.0.0 or later.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>a11ied/browser</code><span>For Vitest browser mode: <code>screenReader({'{'} container {'}'})</code> and <code>queuedScreenReader({'{'} container {'}'})</code> over the mounted component, the same matchers, and the same queued <code>sr</code> fixture.</span></div>
      </div>
      <p>
         <code>await using</code> stops the reader when the block ends, so no <code>try</code> and
         <code>finally</code> is needed. On a queued reader it also runs the commands still in the
         queue. The <a href="/guides/vitest">Vitest guide</a> has a test file to copy and the
         browser mode configuration.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="driver">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Driver</p>
         <h2>Start and drive a session</h2>
      </div>
      <pre><code>import {'{'}
  attachDocumentToDriverSession,
  resolveDocumentTarget,
  runDriverSessionAction,
  startDriverSession,
  stopDriverSession,
{'}'} from 'a11ied';

const url = 'http://localhost:3000/checkout';
const target = await resolveDocumentTarget({'{'} url {'}'});

await startDriverSession({'{'} target: 'virtual' {'}'});
await attachDocumentToDriverSession({'{'} html: await target.readHtml(), url {'}'});

try {'{'}
  const result = await runDriverSessionAction({'{'} action: 'next', payload: {'{'} kind: 'heading' {'}'} {'}'});

  console.log(result.state.lastSpokenPhrase);
  console.log(result.state.transcript);
{'}'} finally {'{'}
  await stopDriverSession();
{'}'}</code></pre>
      <p>
         <code>startDriverSession</code>'s <code>url</code> option only records where the
         session came from. It does not fetch a page or open a browser for you.
      </p>
      <p>
         For a virtual session, call <code>attachDocumentToDriverSession</code> with the markup,
         as shown above. For a real target, open the page yourself first, since VoiceOver
         and NVDA read whatever is already on screen. <code>a1 sr start</code> and
         <code>screenReader</code> from <code>a11ied/test</code> both do this work for you.
      </p>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><code>startDriverSession(options?)</code><span>Takes <code>target</code>, <code>mode</code>, <code>engine</code>, <code>recordingPath</code>, <code>url</code>, <code>app</code>, <code>idleTimeoutMinutes</code>, and <code>timeoutMs</code>. Returns the new <code>session</code> and, when one was already running, the <code>replacedSession</code> it stopped.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>runDriverSessionAction(request, options?)</code><span>The request is a <code>DriverActionRequestInput</code>, typed per action: <code>{'{'} action: 'next' {'}'}</code>, <code>{'{'} action: 'press', payload: {'{'} keys: ['Tab', 'Tab'] {'}'} {'}'}</code>, <code>{'{'} action: 'goto', payload: {'{'} role: 'button' {'}'} {'}'}</code>. A payload of the wrong shape does not compile, and payload fields with defaults, such as <code>max</code>, can be left out.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>getDriverSessionStatus(options?)</code><span>Read the session state without moving the cursor.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>attachDocumentToDriverSession(document, options?)</code><span>Point the session at another page.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>runEphemeralDriverAction(options)</code><span>One action in a session that is torn down before the call returns.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>stopDriverSession(options?)</code><span>Stop the driver, finish any recording, and delete the state file.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>getActiveDriverSession()</code><span>The active session, or <code>undefined</code> when the broker behind it is gone.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>buildDriverTranscript(session, entries)</code><span>Build the transcript document. <code>formatTranscript</code> renders it, and <code>writeDriverTranscript</code> writes it to a file.</span></div>
      </div>
      <p>
         These are the functions the CLI runs. One session is active per user, so no function takes
         a session id, and a session started with <code>mode: 'broker'</code> lives in its own
         process until <code>stopDriverSession</code> or <code>idleTimeoutMinutes</code>, which
         defaults to 30.
      </p>
      <p>
         A test should use <code>screenReader</code> from <code>a11ied/test</code> instead: it
         owns the lifecycle and disposes the session with the test.
      </p>
      <p>
         Every action result includes <code>session.engine</code> for a virtual session and
         <code>state.transcript</code>: an array of entries with an <code>index</code>, an ISO
         <code>at</code> timestamp, the <code>phrase</code>, the <code>itemText</code> when the
         reader reported one, and a <code>checkpoint</code> label on the entries
         <code>checkpoint</code> added.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="axe">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">axe</p>
         <h2>Run axe against a URL</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
         <code>runAxe</code> runs axe-core (axe), an open-source rules engine that checks a page
         against a set of automated accessibility rules, and returns the raw result.
      </p>
      <pre><code>import {'{'} runAxe {'}'} from 'a11ied';

const result = await runAxe(
  {'{'} kind: 'goto', url: 'http://localhost:3000/checkout' {'}'},
  {'{'} wcagVersion: '2.2', level: 'AA' {'}'},
);

for (const violation of result.violations) {'{'}
  console.log(violation.id, violation.impact, violation.nodes[0]?.target);
{'}'}</code></pre>
      <p>
         The first argument is a <code>DocumentLoad</code>: <code>&#123; kind: 'goto', url &#125;</code>
         for a page Playwright navigates to, or <code>&#123; kind: 'html', html &#125;</code> for inline
         markup. <code>resolveDocumentTarget</code> builds one from a URL, a file path,
         <code>-</code> for stdin, or <code>&#123; html &#125;</code>, the same way the CLI resolves its
         positional target.
      </p>
      <p>
         Scope the run with <code>level</code>, <code>criterion</code>, or <code>ruleIds</code>. The
         options type allows one of the three. Omit all three to run every rule mapped in the WCAG
         version.
      </p>
      <p>
         The result has <code>violations</code>, <code>passes</code>, <code>incomplete</code>,
         <code>inapplicable</code>, the resolved <code>ruleIds</code>, and a
         <code>selection</code> object that says how the rule list was chosen.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="wcag">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Standards</p>
         <h2>Look up criteria and coverage</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
         These functions read the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG), the standard most
         accessibility requirements come from, one success criterion at a time. A success
         criterion is a numbered, testable requirement such as <code>4.1.3</code>, assigned a
         conformance level of A, AA, or AAA.
      </p>
      <pre><code>import {'{'}
  listWcagCriteria,
  searchWcagCriteria,
  showWcagTestMethod,
  showWcagCriterion,
{'}'} from 'a11ied';

const status = showWcagCriterion('4.1.3', '2.2');

console.log(status.criterion.title, status.testMethod.method);

const {'{'} testMethod, strategy {'}'} = showWcagTestMethod('4.1.3', '2.2');

if (strategy.requiresRealTarget) {'{'}
  console.log('Needs a driver session:', strategy.procedureIds);
{'}'}

const levelAA = listWcagCriteria('AA', '2.2');
const matches = searchWcagCriteria('focus order', {'{'} version: '2.2', limit: 3 {'}'});</code></pre>
      <p>
         These functions read data bundled with the package, so they make no network request,
         except <code>showWcagAxeRule</code>, the one asynchronous lookup.
      </p>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><code>showWcagCriterion</code><span>Returns the criterion with its <code>coverage</code> and <code>strategy</code>.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>listWcagCriteria</code><span>Takes <code>undefined</code> as the level to return every criterion.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>showWcagTechnique('G18', '2.2')</code><span>Resolves a technique or failure ID to the criteria that list it.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>showWcagCoverageSummary('2.2')</code><span>Returns the coverage totals per level.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>showWcagAxeRule('color-contrast', '2.2')</code><span>Maps an axe rule ID to its criteria, and reads the help text from the installed axe-core.</span></div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="inspect">
      <h2>Relevant criteria</h2>
      <pre><code>import {'{'} inspectRelevantCriteriaUrl, inspectCriterionUrl {'}'} from 'a11ied';

const matrix = await inspectRelevantCriteriaUrl('http://localhost:3000', '2.2');
const focusOrder = await inspectCriterionUrl('2.4.3', 'http://localhost:3000', '2.2');

console.log(focusOrder.assessment.state);
console.log(focusOrder.assessment.reasons);</code></pre>
      <p>
         Both fetch the URL and parse the returned HTML. Use
         <code>inspectRelevantCriteriaTarget</code> and <code>inspectCriterionTarget</code> when
         you already have a resolved document target rather than a URL.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="doctor">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Runtime</p>
         <h2>Check the host</h2>
      </div>
      <pre><code>import {'{'} createDoctorReport, renderDoctorText, resolveAvailableDefaultTarget {'}'} from 'a11ied';

const report = createDoctorReport();
const stepsLeft = report.actions.filter((action) => {'{'} return action.required; {'}'});

console.log(report.ready, stepsLeft);
console.log(renderDoctorText(report));

const {'{'} target, targetType, warning {'}'} = await resolveAvailableDefaultTarget();</code></pre>
      <p>
         <code>resolveAvailableDefaultTarget</code> checks whether the platform screen reader is
         ready for automation and falls back to <code>virtual</code> when it is not. The returned
         <code>warning</code> is set on every fallback.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="ledger" id="exports">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Exports</p>
         <h2>Export map</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Tests</strong><span><code>a11ied/test</code>: <code>screenReader</code>, <code>queuedScreenReader</code>, <code>queueScreenReader</code>, <code>ScreenReader</code>, <code>ScreenReaderAssertionError</code>. <code>a11ied/vitest</code> and <code>a11ied/browser</code>: <code>test</code>, <code>it</code>, <code>screenReaderMatchers</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Sessions</strong><span><code>startDriverSession</code>, <code>getDriverSessionStatus</code>, <code>runDriverSessionAction</code>, <code>runEphemeralDriverAction</code>, <code>stopDriverSession</code>, <code>attachDocumentToDriverSession</code>, <code>cleanupStaleDriverSessions</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Commands</strong><span><code>listDriverCommands</code>, <code>resolveDriverCommand</code>, <code>driverCommandSets</code>, <code>isDriverCommandSet</code>, <code>parseDriverCommandSet</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>axe</strong><span><code>runAxe</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>WCAG</strong><span><code>listWcagCriteria</code>, <code>showWcagCriterion</code>, <code>searchWcagCriteria</code>, <code>showWcagTestMethod</code>, <code>showWcagTestMethodSummary</code>, <code>showWcagTechnique</code>, <code>showWcagAxeRule</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Relevant criteria</strong><span><code>inspectRelevantCriteriaTarget</code>, <code>inspectRelevantCriteriaUrl</code>, <code>inspectCriterionTarget</code>, <code>inspectCriterionUrl</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Page and screen reader selection</strong><span><code>resolveDocumentTarget</code>, <code>openUrlInSystemAutomationBrowser</code>, <code>resolveDefaultTarget</code>, <code>resolveAvailableDefaultTarget</code>, <code>resolveTargetType</code>, <code>listSupportedTargets</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Diagnostics</strong><span><code>createDoctorReport</code>, <code>renderDoctorText</code>, <code>listCliCommands</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Errors</strong><span><code>CliUsageError</code>, <code>CliEnvironmentError</code>, <code>DriverCommandError</code></span></div>
      </div>
      <p>
         The package also exports the option and result types, including
         <code>AxeRunOptions</code>, <code>ScreenReaderOptions</code>,
         <code>QueuedScreenReader</code>, <code>CommandQueueOptions</code>,
         <code>StartDriverSessionOptions</code>, <code>DriverCommandList</code>, and
         <code>TargetType</code>.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="packages">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Packages</p>
         <h2>The @a11ied packages</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
         <code>a11ied</code> re-exports the public core helpers and is the package to depend on.
         Install a scoped package only when you need a lower-level API it does not re-export.
      </p>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><code>@a11ied/contracts</code><span>Zod schemas and result types shared across the runtime.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>@a11ied/core</code><span>WCAG lookup, target resolution, driver orchestration, axe runs, doctor reports.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>@a11ied/guidepup</code><span>Platform adapters for VoiceOver, NVDA, and the virtual reader.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>@a11ied/wcag-data</code><span>Upstream data sync and the generated artifacts.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>@a11ied/wcag-engine</code><span>Lookup, search, coverage, and applicability over those artifacts.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>@a11ied/mcp-server</code><span>The MCP server entrypoint.</span></div>
      </div>
   </section>
</DocShell>
